A self-signed issuer and a certificate from it, to see it work:

  kubectl apply -f - <<'EOF'
  apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
  kind: ClusterIssuer
  metadata: {name: selfsigned}
  spec: {selfSigned: {}}
  ---
  apiVersion: cert-manager.io/v1
  kind: Certificate
  metadata: {name: example, namespace: default}
  spec:
    secretName: example-tls
    dnsNames: [example.ferry.test]
    issuerRef: {name: selfsigned, kind: ClusterIssuer}
  EOF
  kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready certificate/example

The webhook needs the API server to reach a pod, which it does here because the
Mac is on the pod network. ACME issuers need the challenge reachable from the
internet, which a laptop usually is not; DNS-01 works where HTTP-01 cannot.

Disabling removes the CRDs, and with them every Certificate and Issuer.
